bugs for OS-9/68000===================ORIG holds comp.sources.games volume 13, dr_mario, as posted: BUGS I 1.3,a Dr. Mario lookalike.  mario.shr is the submission mail with the samefiles inside.  The files beside ORIG build the OS-9 program, named bugsas its Makefile names it.What changed, and why:  main.c   The game made standard input non-blocking with fcntl()'s  info.h   FNDELAY, so that wgetch() returned EOF when no key was waiting  loop.c   and the pieces fell on their own.  Under OSK bleed() sets a flag           instead, and the game's key read, bugs_wgetch(), asks _gs_rdy()           first and returns EOF when nothing is waiting.           SIGTSTP does not exist here and is not caught.  info.h   The globals were defined in every file, which BSD's linker  main.c   merges and l68 rejects; under OSK main.c defines them and the           other files declare them extern.  loop.c   usleep() was built on select(); under OSK it is tsleep() with           the high bit set, which counts in 256ths of a second.  recipe   -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand: the default libraries have no           random().meat.c and startup.c build unchanged.Measured: the level and speed prompts take j, k and Return; the piecesfall while no key is pressed; h and l move a piece and a and s turn it;q ends the game.Build: cc main.c startup.c loop.c meat.c -DOSK -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand          -l=curses.l -l=termlib.l